Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:37:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [Fix] marlin: Prevent scale underflow in NVFP4 fallback
 on SM80-SM90 (#44998)

When NVFP4 checkpoints have small block scales (e.g. weight_scale_2 = 1.0 from ModelOpt, probec, or llm-compressor), (scales * 2^7).view(int16) << 1 underflows the exponent bits during BF16 dequantization because scale * 2^7 < 2.

Port vllm-project/vllm#34577:
- Add _nvfp4_compute_scale_factor to compute power-of-2 rescaling factor
- Apply rescaling and clamp subnormals in nvfp4_marlin_process_scales
- Divide weight_global_scale by scale_factor in prepare_nvfp4_layer_for_marlin
- Unify scale_factor across experts in prepare_moe_nvfp4_layer_for_marlin and adjust global scale
- Add unit tests for dense and MoE scale factor handling and underflow prevention

Signed-off-by: DEV TYAGI <devtyagi3909@gmail.com>
